# sentence-transformers (below) pulls in torch as a transitive dependency.
# This service runs CPU-only — the embedding model here is a small
# sentence-transformer used for RAG similarity search (app/rag/
# vector_store.py), never anything GPU-bound — but PyPI's default `torch`
# wheel bundles the full CUDA toolkit as separate `nvidia-*` packages
# (~3-5GB across ~15 packages: cublas, cudnn, cusolver, nccl, etc.), none
# of which this process will ever load. That bloat turns into a real
# problem on a PaaS build (Render, Railway, etc.): multi-GB image pulls,
# slow builds, and on cheaper plans, a real chance of hitting a disk quota.
# The extra index below serves torch's CPU-only wheels instead — same
# API, no CUDA payload. Requires regenerating requirements.txt from a
# network context that can actually reach download.pytorch.org (this
# repo's CI runners can; some sandboxed dev environments can't) via:
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements.txt requirements.in
# After regenerating, grep the result for `^nvidia-` — if anything still
# matches, the resolver picked the CUDA build off PyPI instead of the CPU
# build off the extra index (pip/uv don't strictly prioritize one index
# over another for a same-named, same-version package), and torch needs
# an explicit `==<version>+cpu` pin here to force it.
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
